Debug.Assert(OLD(_items.Length) == _size + x);
</code>
To access the value of `_items.Length` (the original length of the internal array), we can use the `OLD()` syntax. The assert statement checks if the original length of the internal array is equal to the sum of the current size and `x`, which represents the number of elements being added to the list.

Note that the original length of the internal array is calculated before the elements are added to the list. Therefore, it is necessary to use `OLD(_items.Length)` instead of `_items.Length` to ensure that the correct length is used for the assertion.--------------------